{{Quote|I know the Muuns to be a good and honest people, and that it is the actions of only these unscrupulous few who are responsible.|Rush Clovis|<ref name="Rise of Clovis">{{TCW|The Rise of Clovis}}</ref>}}
'''Muuns''' were a thin, tall [[humanoid]] [[species]] with elongated heads who ran the [[InterGalactic Banking Clan]] throughout the waning days of the [[Galactic Republic]] and into the [[New Republic Era]]. [[Dark Lord of the Sith|Dark Lord]] of the [[Sith]], [[Darth Plagueis]] was a Muun.

==Biology and appearance==
The Muuns were a tall, pale humanoid species, known commonly across the galaxy as greed-driven [[banker]]s. The species' elongated skulls added to their height. Muuns hairless heads featured small [[eye]]s over a long, shallow [[nose]], often giving their speech a nasal quality. Their small ears were also flat, and were found underneath their skullcap. Their thin arms were of normal length, featuring five-digit hands. The last two fingers of their hands were much shorter than the others.<ref name="Crisis at the Heart" /> Unlike some other [[humanoid]] species, in Muuns females did not possess prominent [[breast]]s.<ref name="SC 105">{{SkeletonCrew|You Have a Lot to Learn About Pirates}}</ref><ref name="SC 105 ST">{{SkeletonCrew|You Have a Lot to Learn About Pirates}} {{Subtitles|Disney+}}</ref> Underneath their slim waist were a pair of very long, thin legs.<ref name="Crisis at the Heart" /> They were a very intelligent species, known to have incredible mathematical capabilities. This was especially utilized in the management of the [[InterGalactic Banking Clan]].<ref name="Visual Encyclopedia" />

The average Muun was just under 2 [[meter]]s tall.<ref name="Endless Vigil" /> Individual Muuns were known to be as tall as 2.46 meters in the case of [[Nix Card]].<ref name="Join the Battle">''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars: Character Encyclopedia - Join the Battle!]]''</ref> The species were able to have a connection to [[the Force]], and use it.<ref name="Endless Vigil" />

==History==
[[File:Plagueis-TheAcolyte.png|thumb|right|200px|Darth Plagueis the Wise, a notable Muun Sith Lord]]
Muuns [[Homeworld|hailed]] from the [[planet]] [[Muunilinst]] in the [[Outer Rim Territories]].<ref name="BMF45" /> The Muuns controlled the InterGalactic Banking Clan<ref name="PoP">{{TCW|Pursuit of Peace}}</ref> and constructed their empire high amidst [[Water|snowy]] [[mountain]] peaks.<ref name="Visual Encyclopedia" /> [[Senator]] [[Rush Clovis]] was raised by a family of Muuns.<ref name="Crisis at the Heart" />

Sometime prior to [[132 BBY]],<ref>"Lost/Found" Episode Guide | The Acolyte on [[StarWars.com]] {{C|backup link}} states that the events of ''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte]]'' take place 100 [[Standard year|years]] before the events of [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']], which ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates to [[32 BBY]]. Therefore, ''The Acolyte'' takes place in [[132 BBY]].</ref> a Muun individual was trained by the [[Dark Lord of the Sith]] [[Darth Tenebrous]]<ref>[[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon 44|''Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon'' 44]] {{C|[[Starship Fact File]]: Sith Infiltrator–Scimitar}}</ref> and took on the moniker of [[Darth Plagueis]].<ref name=":0">{{Film|III}}</ref> After replacing Tenebrous as the [[Sith Master]], Plagueis went on to acquire [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]] as his [[Sith apprentice|apprentice]] with the title [[Darth]] Sidious, and the two would work together to further their order’s [[Grand Plan|grand plan]] of infiltrating and supplanting the [[Galactic Republic]] with a revived [[Sith Empire]].<ref>Darth Sidious Biography Gallery in the [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]]</ref> Plagueis also studied the nature of [[the Force]], both in experiments with [[midi-chlorian]]s<ref name="The Star Wars Book">''[[The Star Wars Book]]''</ref> and research into the [[Doctrine of the Dyad]] and [[transference]],<ref name="Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: Expanded Edition">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: Expanded Edition]]''</ref> in hopes of uncovering the secret to [[immortality]].<ref name="Star Wars: The Secrets of the Sith">''[[Star Wars: The Secrets of the Sith]]''</ref> He ultimately failed in this quest but succeeded in arranging for Palpatine’s rise to political power.<ref name="Star Wars: Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> By [[32 BBY]]<ref>In [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']], [[Jedi Master]] [[Yoda]] states that there could only be two [[Sith Lord]]s at a [[time]]; a [[Rule of Two]] was in place of [[Sith]]<nowiki/>succession, as explained in the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' episode "[[Sacrifice (episode)|Sacrifice]]." Since [[Darth Sidious]] and [[Maul|Darth Maul]] were the two [[Dark Lord of the Sith|Dark Lords]] during ''The Phantom Menace'', which ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates to [[32 BBY]], and that Darth Plagueis was Sidious' [[Sith Master]] according to [[StarWars.com]]'s [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]], Plagueis would have to have been the Sith alongside his [[Sith apprentice|apprentice]] before the title of [[Darth]], and hence the mantle of succeeding the remaining place of the Rule of Two, was conferred to Maul, which had been so by the events of ''The Phantom Menace'', in 32 BBY.</ref> he had taught his apprentice everything he knew, by which point Sidious killed him in his sleep.<ref name=":0" />

During the [[Clone Wars]], both the Galactic Republic and the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] spent large amounts of [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]] on soldiers and weapons for the war.<ref name="PoP">{{TCW|Pursuit of Peace}}</ref> The human Clovis spent time representing the organization in the [[Galactic Senate]]<ref name="Senate Spy">{{TCW|Senate Spy}}</ref> and was replaced by [[Nix Card]] upon his fall from grace.<ref name="Join the Battle" /> Upon his return to political life, Clovis became the head of the IGBC after their ruling body, the [[Core Five]], were arrested for corruption. Clovis was backed by [[Mak Plain]],<ref name="Rise of Clovis" /> but was killed during the [[Invasion of Scipio|Battle of Scipio]].<ref name="Crisis at the Heart">{{TCW|Crisis at the Heart}}</ref> [[San Hill]] was a Muun who was [[Chairman]] of the IGBC and also served on the [[Executive Separatist Council|Separatist Council]]<ref name="Attack of the Clones">{{Film|II}}</ref> until his [[death]] at the [[Mission to Mustafar|end]] of the war.<ref name="Revenge of the Sith">{{Film|III}}</ref>

[[File:Femalemuun.jpg|thumb|left|250px|A bare-chested Muun relaxing in a mud bath]]
During the [[New Republic Era]], Muuns continued their work for the Banking Clan.<ref name="SC 105" /> Around [[9 ABY]],<ref>{{SkeletonCrewDate}}</ref> a few Muun individuals formally visited to the planet [[Lanupa]], staying at<ref name="SC 105" /> [[Skull Ridge Mountain Hotel & Spa]].<ref>{{Getty|url=thewaltdisneystudios/allaccess/#!asset/bj8gqtnvm799njt6mjc6t|text=GR-FF-001420|date=2024-12-23}}</ref> In their free time, several Muuns—including<ref name="SC 105" /> a [[Unidentified male Muun|male]] and a [[Unidentified female Muun|female]]<ref name="SC 105 ST" />—relaxed in a mud [[bath]].<ref name="SC 105" />

